// point_cloud.mat — Epic 3 Task 6 (VM-035). A point cloud's per-point
// color IS the signal (STANDING directive 2026-09-09), so this is UNLIT --
// PBR shading would add a light-direction term nobody asked for and that
// no `PointVertex` (position + packed rgba, no tangent frame -- points have
// no meaningful normal) could feed anyway.
//
// `requires : [ color ]`: the per-point rgba8 point_cloud.cpp's
// PointVertex carries, baked ONCE by the node-side adapter (scene.h's
// PointCloudPoint::rgba) and never re-baked.
//
// `blending : fade` is load-bearing: fade/transparent are what put a
// renderable in the blended queue at all -- an opaque material discards
// vertex/fragment alpha outright (same contract as clay_faded.mat and
// clay_translucent.mat; history in the plan's Task 6 Step 2).
//
// `alpha` is a UNIFORM, not a re-baked vertex attribute: staleness_alpha()
// recomputes every frame during the ~0.5s fade ramp, and rebuilding the
// whole point-cloud vertex buffer every frame to re-bake alpha -- on the
// largest geometry in the scene -- is rejected outright. The per-point
// rgba stays exactly as baked by the adapter (color only); the fade is
// carried entirely by this one float parameter, set once per frame on the
// SINGLE MaterialInstance the whole PointCloudLayer shares (point_cloud.cpp
// -- no per-entity instancing, no rebuild, negligible cost regardless of
// point count).
// `pointSizePx` (user report 2026-09-09: "I can't see any point cloud!"):
// a POINTS primitive rasterizes at gl_PointSize, which defaults to 1px --
// invisible dust at 720p. Set from the theme's point_cloud.point_size_px
// token (soft-defaulted, STANDING directive: style is configurable).
material {
    name : point_cloud,
    shadingModel : unlit,
    parameters : [
        { type : float, name : alpha },
        { type : float, name : pointSizePx }
    ],
    requires : [ color ],
    blending : fade
}
vertex {
    void materialVertex(inout MaterialVertexInputs material) {
        gl_PointSize = materialParams.pointSizePx;
    }
}
fragment {
    void material(inout MaterialInputs material) {
        prepareMaterial(material);
        material.baseColor.rgb = getColor().rgb;
        material.baseColor.a = materialParams.alpha;
    }
}
